      "text": "To determine the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to US dollars.\n2. Convert the cost of the painting from US dollars to Chinese yuan.\n\nFirst, let's find out how much the painting costs in US dollars. We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars. Therefore, to find out how many US dollars are equivalent to 105 Namibian dollars, we can set up the following conversion:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{\\text{Cost in Namibian dollars}}{\\text{Exchange rate}} = \\frac{105}{7} = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n\\]\n\nNext, we convert the cost from US dollars to Chinese yuan. We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan. Therefore, to find out how many Chinese yuan are equivalent to 15 US dollars, we can set up the following conversion:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = \\text{Cost in US dollars} \\times \\text{Exchange rate} = 15 \\times 6 = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n\\]\n\nThus, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\boxed{90}.",
